.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt ATD 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm atd
.Nd minimal at scheduler
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon scans
.Pa /var/at
once per second, parses every regular
.Pa *.job
file and runs due jobs through the kernel spawn path.
.Pp
Each job logs
.Dq atd: start
with the job id and command, then
.Dq atd: exit
with the id and status.
A job is retired after the run attempt, including a failed spawn, so a
broken command does not retry forever.
On a filesystem without unlink the job becomes a hidden
.Dq due=-1
tombstone instead of being removed.
.Pp
Regular jobs run before batch jobs.
A batch job runs only on a tick with no due regular job;
the kernel has no load-average source, so an idle tick is the low-load proxy.
The scheduler is
serial and never starts one job twice concurrently.
.Pp
The spool persists across a restart: pending jobs are found again by the next scan.
Removal
after a run attempt is not atomic with the spawn, so a crash in that window can repeat a job.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/at -compact
.It Pa /var/at
Job spool.
The image must mount a writable filesystem there.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
runs until terminated.
It exits non-zero only on an unrecoverable startup error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr at 1 ,
.Xr batch 1
.Sh STANDARDS
This daemon implements the
.Nm at
queue described in
.Xr at 1 .
Multi-line scripts, shell metacharacters and true load-average batch scheduling are
unsupported.
